#30346
old man sage whitebeard white bearded~
a white-bearded old man~
A white-bearded old man sits between the twin fires and says, "Eastmost peninsula is the secret."
~
His beard is so long and white that he has tucked the end of it into his
belt to keep it from the flames on either side of him. He speaks slowly, as
though every word costs him something, and he says only the one thing. Ask
what he means and he turns his face east, lifts a finger a little toward
the north where the land runs out into the water, then rubs finger and
thumb together like a man counting coins. Whatever waits out there, he
thinks it worth a hundred rupees.
~
human~
