#30348
old man sage squinter squinting~
a squinting old man~
A squinting old man leans close and asks, "Did you get the sword from the old man on top of the waterfall?"
~
He squints at everyone, and at you he squints hardest, measuring the blade
you carry against some better one he has in mind. A kinsman of his keeps a
white sword in a cave high up where the river tumbles out of the hills, he
says, and gives it only to those whose hearts are many enough to bear it.
He asks after that old man as though after a brother he has not seen in
years, and looks disappointed if you have not yet made the climb.
~
