#30349
old man sage damp robed~
a damp-robed old man~
A damp-robed old man wrings out his sleeve and murmurs, "Walk into the waterfall."
~
His robe is wet to the knees and never seems to dry, though the fires on
either side of him burn hot enough. He will not say where he has been, only
that a curtain of falling water is not always a wall. Somewhere in the
hills the river drops over a cliff, and behind it, he hints, an old woman
keeps a dry little room and sells what she knows for coin. He thinks she
charges far too much, and says so, but he keeps going back.
~
