#30350
old man sage deaf half~
a half-deaf old man~
A half-deaf old man cups a hand to his ear and shouts, "Digdogger hates certain kind of sound."
~
He is nearly deaf, and so he shouts everything, then winces at the echo.
Long ago, he explains at the top of his voice, he learned that some noises
hurt more than any blade, and that the great eye called Digdogger, which
haunts these halls, cannot abide a certain tune. If you carry something
that plays one, he hints, this is the place to put it to your lips. He hums
a few bars, very badly, to make his point.
~
