#30351
old man sage fletcher trimming feathers~
an old man trimming feathers~
An old man trimming feathers glances up from his work and says, "Secret power is said to be in the arrow."
~
A heap of grey feathers lies about his knees, and he trims them one at a
time with a little knife, fitting each to a shaft that he never quite
finishes. An arrow is more than a point and a string, he tells you. The
hopping, long-eared things that haunt these halls, the pols voices, fall to
a single one of them where a sword must hack and hack. He offers no arrows
of his own; he only says you will be glad of a bow down here.
~
