#30352
old man bagmaker fidgety~
a fidgety old man~
A fidgety old man rubs his hands together and grins, "I bet you'd like to have more bombs."
~
He cannot keep still: his fingers drum, his feet tap and his eyes keep
straying to the bags heaped behind him, each stitched with a double seam.
He is a bag-maker, he explains, and proud of it, and his bags carry four
more bombs than the one at your hip. One costs 100 rupees, and you may BUY
BAG to have it, though he will sell each traveller only one. Once he has
your coin he talks happily about powder until you leave.
~
