#30354
old man sage wistful~
a wistful old man~
A wistful old man gazes into the flames and sighs, "There are secrets where fairies don't live."
~
He speaks of fairies the way other men speak of old sweethearts, gazing
into the fire as he does. Every pond in Hyrule has its fairy, he says, or
ought to, and it troubles him that one lake does not. A water so empty of
them must be keeping something else, he hints, something that might answer
to music played upon its shore. He hums a tune under his breath, loses the
thread of it, and starts again from the beginning.
~
