old man sage hooknose hook nosed~
a hook-nosed old man~
A hook-nosed old man taps the end of his long nose and whispers, "There's a secret in the tip of the nose."
~
His nose is the largest thing about him, long and hooked and red at the
tip, and he taps it often. These halls, he says, were cut by someone with a
sense of humour: walk them with a map in your head and they make a face,
horned and grinning, with a great nose in the middle. Look hard at the very
end of that nose, he hints, tapping his own once more. He finds the whole
idea far funnier than you are likely to.
~
