old woman crone sharp eyed~
a sharp-eyed old woman~
A sharp-eyed old woman holds out a wrinkled palm and says, "Pay me and I'll talk."
~
Her eyes are small and black and miss nothing, least of all the purse at
your belt. She knows things, she says, and knowledge is a trade like any
other. GIVE her rupees and she will talk accordingly. 10 rupees is an
insult, and she will tell you so. 30 buys the way through the Lost Woods,
where travellers walk in circles for days. 50, she admits with a cackle,
buys nothing but her opinion of how rich you must be.
~
