old woman crone misty mist soaked~
a mist-soaked old woman~
A mist-soaked old woman wrings out her shawl and grumbles, "Pay me and I'll talk."
~
The roar of the falls fills her little room behind the curtain of water,
and her shawl is always damp with spray. She grumbles about the cold, about
her knees and about travellers who expect something for nothing. GIVE her
rupees if you want her to talk: 5 or 10 will not open her mouth, but 20
buys the way up through the Lost Hills, which turn back anyone who climbs
them blind. She counts every coin twice.
~
