old man sage leathery~
a leathery old man~
A leathery old man squints into the distance and drawls, "Secret is in the tree at the dead-end."
~
Years of sun have tanned him to the colour and texture of an old saddle,
and he speaks slowly, as if he has all afternoon. Out where a path runs to
nothing, he says, a single tree stands by itself, and it has always struck
him as standing guard over something. Wood, he hints, makes a poor door
against a flame. He pulls a dry twig from his pocket and turns it
thoughtfully in the firelight.
~
