He has a long, sharp nose and uses it to sniff out how much money a
customer is carrying, or so he claims. His shop sits high in the hills, and
he charges for the climb: a Magical Shield at 160 rupees, a small Key at
100 and a Blue Candle at 60. The candle, he says, sees off the dark and the
brambles alike. LIST shows his stock and BUY puts an end to the sniffing.
He knows the price of everything.
~
