the great fairy of the woods~
The great fairy of the woods hovers above the still pond, trailing motes of light.
~
She is no taller than your hand, wrapped in a glow like sunlight through
green leaves, and she dances over the pond on wings that blur and hum. She
does not speak, but she laughs, a sound like a little bell. Anyone who
comes to rest at her pond, so long as they are not fighting, finds their
hearts made whole: wounds close, strength returns, and weary legs feel
fresh again. She asks nothing in return, and seems pleased simply to be
visited.
~
