#31014
octorok blue~
a blue octorok~
A blue octorok clings to the cliff edge, crusted white with salt.
~
Sea wind has scoured this octorok to a faded slate blue, and a rime of
dried salt crusts its rubbery hide around the eyes and snout. It lives on
the cliff tops where gulls wheel, and it has learned to spit its stones
downwind so the gale carries them farther and faster than any shot on the
lowland grass. Only a shield turned to meet them will stop them, and it
needs many heavy cuts to fall.
~
