a blue octorok~
A blue octorok lurks among the tide pools, barnacles on its back.
~
Barnacles have taken root along the back of this old octorok, and one of
its four legs ends in a healed stump from some fight among the tide pools
of the southeastern coast. It moves in a rolling, lopsided scuttle but has
lost none of its speed, and the stones it spits are lumps of beach rock
that ring off a shield like a hammer on an anvil. It shrugs off blows that
would burst younger kin.
~
