The largest of its kind for leagues, this octorok has grown a hide so dark
it is nearly black, rippled with old scars where swords once bit and failed
to finish it. It holds a stretch of the southern paths as its own and has
spat so many stones there that they lie scattered like hail. Each shot
comes out with the force of a sling bullet, and only a raised shield keeps
a skull whole against it.
