This one is barely grown, its red bristles still patchy over pink hide and
its ears too big for its head. It has made a nest of snapped arrows and
stolen bones beneath the thicket's knotted roots and guards it with a
short, crooked spear. When it spots a stranger it yaps, rears back and
hurls the spear in a straight line, and a raised shield turns the throw
aside with a dull clack.
