#30201
Southwest Meadow~
A wide meadow of tall grass and yellow flowers fills the far southwest
corner of the land, hemmed in by brown rock to the south and west. Some
flower heads spin on their stalks with no wind to turn them. In the western
rock a cave mouth stands open, a thread of smoke curling from it and steps
leading down into firelight. It is a quiet, forgotten corner, and the only
trampled path leads east toward the woods.
~
