#30202
Woodland Rock Face~
Trees crowd against the wall of brown rock that marks the southern edge of
the land, their roots wedged into every crack. Crude stone-headed arrows
lie snapped in the turf, and doglike pawprints circle a trampled patch of
grass. One stretch of the rock face is crazed with fine cracks spreading
from a hollow-sounding center, as if a bomb could open it. Paths lead
north, east and west through the woods.
~
