#30203
Southern Woods~
Old trees stand in rows along the southern edge of the land, set as evenly
as an orchard, their crowns meeting overhead in a leafy roof. The leaf
mould is churned by heavy, clawed feet and littered with broken spear
shafts and gnawed bones where something doglike has made camp. Somewhere
among the trunks a twig cracks. Paths lead north, east and west.
~
