#30204
Path to the Manji~
A narrow trail winds east through the southern forest toward a ring of
trees that grow in a pattern too regular to be natural, set like spokes
around a hub. The birdsong fades and the air grows cooler the farther east
the path goes, and snapped spears in the grass show the way is patrolled.
Other trails branch north and west into the deeper forest.
