#30205
Grove of the Manji~
A ring of tall trees encloses a hushed clearing, and at its center a squat
stone entrance is carved with a turning four-armed cross, the sign of the
Manji. Cold air breathes out of the doorway, smelling of moss and damp
stone. Deep paired dents in the turf show where something long-legged lands
after each leap. Rock walls the clearing south and east, and the only way
out is west.
~
