#30206
Sandy Glade~
A clearing of loose, pale sand opens among the trees, oddly bare where the
forest should be. The sand is rippled and pocked with small round burrow
holes, and every so often a patch of it heaves and spins as though
something were boring up from below. At the glade's edge a low cave mouth
opens in a bank, with steps leading down toward firelight. Paths lead north
into the woods and east toward the hills.
~
