#30207
Crags West of the Start~
Brown rock juts up in jagged ridges just west of a quiet green field, the
ground between them dented in pairs where some long-legged hopping thing
lands hard and springs away again. One rock face is cracked and weak, and a
faint rattle like dice in a cup seems to come from behind it, as if a bomb
would open the way to somebody's game. Paths lead north, east toward the
start, and west into the woods.
