#30208
Meadow East of the Cave~
Open grassland stretches east from the starting hills, dotted with small
boulders and clumps of green bushes. Round pebbles lie strewn across the
grass, some still wet, as though spat from a mouth that lives here. One
bush beside the rocks is dry and brittle, its leaves curling brown, plainly
ready to burn, and a bitter smell of herbs hangs about it. Paths lead
north, east and west.
