#30209
Stone Field~
A field of jumbled grey and brown boulders sprawls along the southern edge
of the land, grass growing in tufts between them. One great stone sits
loose in its bed, ringed by fresh-turned earth and too heavy for any
ordinary arm, as if a bracelet of strength were needed to shift it aside.
Paired dents mark where hopping things have landed among the rocks. The
field opens east and west.
