#30211
Southern Sands~
Sandy ground stretches along the southern edge of the land, rippled by the
wind and pocked with burrow holes that open and close like breathing. Now
and then a spinning red shape bores up through the sand and sinks away
again. To the south rises a rock wall, and one section of it is cracked and
weak, the crackle of a pair of fires sounding faintly behind it as though a
bomb might open a room. Paths lead north, east and west.
