#30213
Southern Shore Path~
A grassy path runs along the southern edge of the land, the low boom of the
sea drifting in from the east. Beside it rises a wall of brown rock, and
one section is cracked and crumbling, hollow-sounding when the wind moans
past. Whoever lives behind it, a bomb would make a door, and a door would
have to be paid for. Small blue-grey stones lie scattered in the grass.
Paths lead east and west.
