#30214
Southeast Grassland~
Wide grassland sweeps toward the southeastern coast, the long grass bent
flat by a constant wind that carries salt from the sea. Small round stones
lie scattered about, some half buried as if spat with force from a snout,
and the turf is torn where something stout and eight-legged scuttles. Gulls
cry somewhere to the east. Paths lead east toward the shore and west across
the grass.
~
