#30216
Western Meadow Edge~
Open meadow runs right up to the western edge of the land, where the grass
stops at a sheer brown bluff. A spinning flower rises and falls on the
wind, and deep, heavy hoofprints cut through the blossoms beside scorched
patches of grass, the trail of something large, four-legged and fire-
breathing that patrols here. Paths lead north toward the rocks and east
into the woods.
~
