#30219
Bramble Wood~
Thorny brambles crowd between the trunks, snagging cloth and skin alike,
and the trail weaves a careful line through them. A bush beside the path
has dried out completely, its leaves brittle and grey, and the ground
behind it rings faintly hollow underfoot. Spat stones and spear shafts lie
together in the thorns. Paths break away through the brambles in all four
directions.
