A tidy line of thick green bushes borders a sunny field, almost like a
hedge someone once planted and forgot. One of them stands out from its
neighbours, dry and brittle, its leaves browned and curled as though it
would go up in flame in an instant, and a new-looking doorframe peeks
between its roots. Worn paths cross the field to the north, south, east and
west.
