Dense bushes crowd the riverbank, their roots trailing into the slow brown
water and their branches heavy with river mist. Among all that green one
bush stands dry and dead, its twigs grey and snapping in the breeze, as
though waiting for a spark, and someone has nailed a little ledger-board to
its trunk. The water swirls where something lurks. Muddy paths lead north,
east and west.
