Tall elms cast deep, cool shade over a quiet grove carpeted in soft moss,
and the birdsong falls silent more often than it should. Near the path one
bush has withered entirely, its brown leaves rattling like paper in the
faintest breeze, and the moss around it is worn by feet that came and went
with full pockets. The grove opens onto trails heading north, south, east
and west.
