underfoot and their branches blotting out much of the sky. The still air
smells of resin and old woodsmoke, and crude spear marks score several
trunks at chest height where something doglike practises its throw. Red-
dyed rags hang from a broken branch. Narrow trails lead north, east and
west between the trees.
