The Lion's Thicket~
A quiet clearing in the eastern forest is empty but for a single bush
standing apart, dry and brittle and rooted in strangely flat, square-cut
stone. Cold air seeps up from beneath its roots, carrying a smell of old
masonry and deep places, and the carved paw of some great stone lion shows
through the grass beside it. A spark would clear the way. Paths lead north,
east and west.
