on the rocks below. In a rocky bank set back from the cliff edge a cave
mouth opens, and a sharp whiff of black powder and lamp oil drifts out to
mingle with the salt air, the smell of a merchant who sells bombs and
arrows. The coast path runs north and south, and a track heads inland to
the west.
