Brown boulders and jagged rock spurs crowd the western edge of the world,
and deep claw marks score the stone beside blackened streaks where
something spat fire. Scattered bones bleach in the sun. To the north a
channel of dark water cuts off the way, wide enough that only a raft could
cross it, while a rough path winds south between the rocks.
