dragonflies hover. Out on the lake a scaly head breaks the surface, glowing
at the throat, and sinks again. A single dry bush grows near the path,
ready to catch the slightest spark, and the turf around it is worn as
though someone small and secretive lives under it. Trails lead north, east
and west.
