A hollow is tucked between low hills, sheltered from the wind and quiet.
Green grass grows thick and undisturbed, and a few old trees stand at its
edges, their roots knotted over smooth river stones. It is one of the few
places in Hyrule where no claw or snout has marked the ground. Paths lead
north and west, and the stillness feels like a held breath.
