#30314
The High Boulder Pass~
Rounded boulders the size of huts crowd this pass, leaving a crooked lane
of bare earth between them. The air is thin and cold, and every sound
bounces back twice from the cliffs. Hoofprints the width of a shield and
singed lichen mark the trail, and a sheer-sided crevice opens in the rock
to the south. The pass runs east and west.
