#30315
Rockfall Crest~
Loose scree pours down from the peaks above, and every so often a fresh
stone comes bounding across the crest with a hollow clatter. The ground is
pocked with craters from earlier falls. In the northern cliff one patch of
rock looks oddly brittle, flaking at a touch, as if a single bomb would
open it, and a narrow crevice cuts the slope to the south. The crest runs
west.
