#30317
Spectacle Rock~
Two great round boulders stand side by side on the summit, joined by a low
saddle of stone like a giant's pair of spectacles left on the mountaintop.
Sand has blown into drifts between them. The left-hand rock sounds hollow
and is seamed with hairline cracks, and the air near it is colder than it
ought to be, as if the way to death itself lay behind. Paths lead east and
west.
