#30318
East of Spectacle Rock~
A broad shelf of packed earth stretches between rows of brown boulders, the
twin humps of Spectacle Rock just visible to the west. Wind-flattened weeds
cling to the cracks, and a few hardy flowers nod in the gusts, one of them
spinning. Scorched hoofprints cross the shelf. Far below, the green of
Hyrule spreads out like a quilt. Paths lead east and west.
