#30319
The Summit Road~
A worn path threads east and west along the mountain's crown, hemmed in by
tumbled boulders and scorched by fiery breath. One face of the cliff shows
a dark crack running from top to bottom, as if a single bomb might open it
on a room someone would charge for. To the south the trail stops at a
narrow crevice with the mountain trail visible beyond.
