#30321
Death Mountain's Dead End~
Boulders close in on every side but the west, forming a still, sheltered
pocket at the top of the world. The silence is heavy after the clatter of
the slopes, and not one fallen stone lies on the ground. Nothing grows here
but grey lichen, the only marks in the dust are the wind's, and the way
back is west.
