#30324
The Candle Merchant's Hollow~
A dip among the high boulders shelters a cave mouth from the worst of the
wind. A whiff of tallow and lamp smoke hangs at the entrance, where candles
and other goods are sold, and the dust before it is scuffed by many feet.
Small craters show where something springs and lands, springs and lands,
all across the hollow. Ways lead east, and a crevice lies south.
