#30325
Tektite Heights~
The rock here is pitted with shallow dents, as though something heavy had
been bouncing across it on long legs for years. Brown cliffs rise to the
north, and one section of them is cracked and crumbling, with a faint
draught whispering out of the seams and a smell of bitter medicine on it. A
narrow crevice divides the heights from the land to the south, and the way
west is open.
