#30330
The Whispering Hearth~
This little cave at the back of the meadow is swept tidy, and a woven mat
lies before the far wall where a visitor is meant to stand and pay. Flower
petals blown in from outside collect in the corners. Two small fires
crackle in iron dishes, and a cracked clay bowl between them holds the odd
rupee left by earlier callers. Stone steps lead up into the meadow.
