#30331
The Cave Behind the Falls~
The roar of the waterfall fills this cave, muffled only a little by the
curtain of water across its mouth, and spray mists the first few yards of
floor. Further in, the stone is dry and two fires burn in hollows cut into
the rock. A flat stone before them is worn smooth and ringed with coin-
sized scratches where payment is laid down. Wet steps climb back up behind
the falls.
