A low-ceilinged chamber of chill teal stone, where bat droppings crust the
tops of a few scattered blocks and a papery rustle drifts down from the
dark. The air tastes of dust. A heavy iron shutter fills the eastern
doorway, dropped by whatever magic keeps this dungeon's halls closed until
they are cleared, and the north door is locked, its keyhole ringed with
rust.
