Level 2: Moonlit Smoke Hollow~
Blue stone closes in on this northeast hollow, damp beading on every block,
but the far end is dry and warm where a pair of fires burns low. Their
smoke curls upward and gathers under the ceiling in a slow grey pall that
never quite clears, and the floor between them is rubbed smooth. A crescent
moon is scratched into one brazier's lip. An open doorway leads south, and
the west wall is fractured and loose, held by old mortar.
