Thick vines and torn, fleshy petals carpet this chamber, heavy with the
sweetness of a monstrous four-headed bloom. Whip-marks and scorch spots
score the floor, and the walls are pitted where the plant rammed itself,
faster each time a head was cut away. A shutter seals the south, the west
wall is cracked, and the door north is locked with the guardian's key.
