A turning cross inlaid in gold marks the centre of this quiet chamber above
the lair, and warm golden light hangs in the air around it. The green stone
is clean, untouched by slime or vine, and a small triangle of light spins
over the cross, a road home for whoever has earned it. An iron-banded chest
stands locked on the cross, and the door south, back into the overgrown
lair, is locked with the guardian's key.
