dark gaps, and it smells of wet timber and pitch. Water drips somewhere
unseen below, and bat droppings spot the ledges. A stone shelf in the gloom
at the far end is where the dungeon's keeper hides his coin, its edge
rubbed smooth by a careful hand. The ladder leads back up.
