The entry hall of the Snake lies beneath its lake island, walls of
glistening blue-green brick carved with coiling serpents whose tails wind
away into the dark. Cold, wet air breathes up from the depths to the north,
and a low side opening leads west into a blacker room. Behind, the stair
climbs back toward daylight and the lap of lake water on the shore.
