Grey brick walls curve gently inward here, and every sound rings back a
moment late, as if the room were listening. Two small fires flicker beside
a worn patch near the north wall, painting the brick orange and drawing a
faint, reedy whistle from the draught that feeds them. Lizard heads are
carved along the skirting. A cracked section of the south wall looks weak,
and the west way stands open.
