Cold air pours down from the mountain's heart into this bare stone
vestibule, carved where the twin crags of Spectacle Rock meet the ground.
The walls are rough, sooty basalt veined with dull red, shaped above the
door into the brow of an enormous skull. Above the north arch eight
triangular sockets are cut, one for every shard of wisdom. A low rumble
comes from the rock itself.
