Scorch marks and a lingering cold presence fill this remote corner room,
set where the eye of the mountain's skull would be. Stone blocks stand in
neat rows, but one sits slightly out of line, with fresh scrapes at its
base and a faint red glow in the crack beneath. The only exit is a cracked
section of the south wall.
